00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Miracle on 34th Street (initially released as The Big Heart in the United Kingdom) is a 1947 American Christmas comedy-drama
film released by 20th Century-Fox, written and directed by George Seaton and based on a story by Valentine Davies.

12
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
It stars Maureen O'Hara, John Payne, Natalie Wood, and Edmund Gwenn.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
The story takes place between Thanksgiving and Christmas in New York City, and focuses on
the effect of a department store Santa Claus who claims to be the real Santa.

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
The film has become a perennial Christmas favorite.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Miracle on 34th Street won three Academy Awards: Gwenn for Best Actor in a Supporting Role, Valentine
Davies for Best Writing, Original Story, and George Seaton for Best Writing, Screenplay.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
The film was nominated for Best Picture, losing to Gentleman's Agreement.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
In 2005, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically or aesthetically significant".

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
The Academy Film Archive preserved Miracle on 34th Street in 2009.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
Davies also wrote a short novelization of the tale, which was published
by Harcourt Brace simultaneously with the film's release.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film explores themes of nanny, christmas, twin.

21
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
